    "body": "With module state, it's possible that the utility code types traverse/clear/dealloc may be called during destructor shutdown when the module state is no longer findable. This is especially an issue for the single-phase init mode, but I think is a general problem.\r\n\r\nThe usual approach we've used in similar situations for heap-types is to bail out and not complete the destruction. For cyfunctions I think we understand the type hierarchy well enough make it work but this may not generally be possible for all types.",
    "closed_at": null,
